   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 138 of the laws of 1998, amending the navigation law\nand the state finance law relating to the operation of personal watercraft and\nspecialty prop-craft, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S10525",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10525-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §8, Chap 138 of 1998",
    "lawSection": "State Finance",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10525\n\nSPONSOR: SERRANO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 138 of the laws of 1998, amending the navigation\nlaw and the state finance law relating to the operation of personal\nwatercraft and specialty prop-craft, in relation to the effectiveness\nthereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the effectiveness of certain provisions of law governing the\noperation of personal watercraft and specialty prop-craft by extending\nthe expiration date of existing requirements.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section $ of chapter 138 of the laws of 1998, as previ-\nously amended, to extend the expiration date of section five of such act\nfrom January 1, 2027 to January I, 2029. The amendment continues the\nphased. applicability of boating safety certificate requirements for\noperators of personal watercraft and specialty prop-craft and preserves\nthe authority of the commissioner of parks, recreation. and historic\npreservation to modify applicable dates by rule or regulation upon a\nfinding that sufficient, courses are not available.\n\nSection 2 provides that the act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe amended language of this bill extends the effectiveness of existing\npersonal watercraft and specialty prop-craft safety provisions to ensure\ncontinuity of operator training and certification requirements. By\nextending the expiration date, the\n  legislation  allows  additional  time for the continued implementation\nand administration of  boating  safety  requirements  while  maintaining\nregulatory flexibility to address course availability.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2024:A.10333 (Jones) /S.9250(SERBANO) - Chapter 191 or 2024\n\n2022:A.9978 (JONES)/S.8955(Serrano) - Chapter 366 of 2022\n\n2021:A.7622 (Jones)/S.2168(Serrano) - Chapter169 of2021\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
